solution:
For a positive integer \(n\), the factorial \(n!\) is the product of the integers from \(1\) through \(n\). First evaluate the factorial inside the parentheses: \(3!=3\cdot2\cdot1=6\). Therefore,
\[
\frac{(3!)!}{3!}
=\frac{6!}{3!}
=\frac{6\cdot5\cdot4\cdot3!}{3!}
=6\cdot5\cdot4=120.
\]
The answer is \(120\), choice \(\mathrm{E}\).

